   "date": "2026-11-10",
   "note": "torch's fp32 linear layers (MKL GEMV) stream only ~25-35 GB/s at batch-1 decode on AMD EPYC, i.e. about one core's worth of bandwidth; OpenBLAS sgemv on the same tensors streams 218-285 GB/s. That the slowdown is inside MKL's AMD code path is a hypothesis (MKL_VERBOSE would show the dispatched kernel).",
   "evidence": "r6615 ctest_r6615: llama3-8b B=1 torch 0.89 tok/s (27 GB/s) vs openblas 9.31 tok/s (284 GB/s); c6525-100g 2026-11-05: every decode row 13-22 GB/s; Intel laptop: torch GEMV at full read rate. BLIS sgemv is as slow as MKL here (llama3-8b B=1: 1.04 tok/s, 32 GB/s), so OpenBLAS is the CPU winner at batch 1."
  },
